,{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SignalBatchStrategy"},{"type":"text","text":" over a stream of the unit’s one value, made afresh"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for each iteration."}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The unit’s work runs in the signal’s task each time iteration begins; a unit that fails","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ends the batched sequence with its error. When the batched sequence ends first, the unit’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"work is cancelled; a unit whose work ignores cancellation keeps the batch’s internal task","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"alive until it returns, though the batched sequence itself ends at once. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SingleValueSubject","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" takes ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/CountBatchStrategy\/signal(_:)-2ind0","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" instead, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leaves the subject alone. Each batched sequence iterated with this strategy runs the unit","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anew and fires once when it completes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Example","anchor":"Example"},{"code":["let reachable = DeferredTask { try await server.waitUntilReachable() }","for try await requests in outbox.batch(strategy: .either(.count(20), .signal(reachable))) {","    try await send(requests)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\